problems.problem:
Two disjoint circles $k_1, k_2$ with centers $O_1$ and $O_2$, respectively, are given in the plane. A common external tangent touches $k_1$ at $A$ and $k_2$ at $B$. Line $O_1O_2$ meets $k_1$ and $k_2$ at $C$ and $D$, respectively. Prove that
(a) points $A, B, C, D$ are concyclic;
(b) lines $AC$ and $BD$ are perpendicular.

Let $A_1A_2A_3A_4$ be a convex quadrilateral whose vertices $A_1,A_2,A_3,A_4$ have affixes $z_1,z_2,z_3,z_4$, respectively, such that:

a) $|z_1|=|z_2|=|z_3|=|z_4|=r$;

b) $|z_1-z_2|=2r$;

c) $\min_{a\in\mathbb{R}}|a\cdot z_1+(1-a)\cdot z_2-z_3|=\frac{1}{2r}\cdot|z_4-z_1|\cdot|z_4-z_2|$.

Show that $A_1A_2A_3A_4$ is an isosceles trapezoid.

The points $M$ and $N$ are the points of tangency of the incircle of the isosceles triangle $ABC$ ($AC=CB$) with the sides $AC$ and $BC$, respectively. The line $l$ is tangent to the minor arc $MN$ of the circle and intersects $NC$ and $MC$ at the points $P$ and $Q$, respectively. Let $AP\cap BQ=\{T\}$. Prove that:

a) the point $T$ belongs to the segment $MN$;

b) the sum of the areas of the triangles $ATQ$ and $BTP$ attains its minimum value when the lines $l$ and $AB$ are parallel.
